{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Dubova, Yang, Yau and Yin, \"Delocalization of two-dimensional random band matrices\" (arXiv:2503.07606). The model is the complex Gaussian block band matrix on the torus Z_L^2 with L^2 blocks of size W x W, N = W^2 L^2, and band width W >= N^c for some c > 0. This entry contains Theorem 2.2 (delocalization of the bulk eigenvectors), Theorem 2.3 (the local semicircle law, (4)-(5)), Theorem 2.4 (generalized quantum unique ergodicity, (8)-(9)) and Theorem 2.5 (quantum diffusion, (10)-(13)); they have no hypotheses other than their parameters, and no result of another work is assumed for them. The library also proves Theorem 2.6 (bulk universality) from one external input, stated as an explicit hypothesis; that theorem is not part of this entry.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
    }
  ],
